Wait — there's an issue in `doUpdateWeightProfile`: it calls `lockBag` then `lockLeg`. Meanwhile `doArrange`/`doLoad`/`doSeal` lock leg first, then bags. Lock ordering inversion: updateWeightProfile locks bag then leg; doArrange locks leg then bag. Potential deadlock under concurrency. To be safe, reorder: in doUpdateWeightProfile, first findBag (no lock) to get loadedLegId, then lock leg if needed, then lock bag. Let me restructure:

```java
BagRow bag = findBag(bagTag);  // no lock
if null 404
LegRow loadedLeg = null;
if (bag.loadedLegId() != null) {
    loadedLeg = lockLeg(bag.loadedLegId());
}
bag = lockBag(bagTag);  // re-read under consistent ordering
...
```

But between findBag and lockLeg, bag could be unloaded (arrange) → loadedLegId null. After locking leg and bag, re-check bag.loadedLegId: if it changed to a different leg... arrange unloads then could load to another leg? No—arrange only affects one leg; bag could be unloaded from leg A and arranged into leg B concurrently. To keep it simple and correct enough: lock in order leg→bag, then verify bag.loadedLegId still equals the locked leg; if it changed, re-evaluate based on current value (if now null → no freeze/pressure checks; if different leg → we don't hold that leg's lock... ). This corner is unlikely in tests. Simpler approach that avoids deadlock: lock bag first is the inversion. Actually which order do other paths use? doLoad: lockLeg then lockBag. doRecover: lockBag only. doArriveDifference: lockLeg then lockBag. So leg→bag is the canonical order. I'll restructure doUpdateWeightProfile to lock leg first (if loaded), then bag, and re-read state after locking.

Rewrite:

```java
private WeightProfileResponse doUpdateWeightProfile(String bagTag, WeightProfileUpdateRequest request) {
    BagRow bag = findBag(bagTag);
    if (bag == null) {
        throw ApiException.notFound("行李不存在: " + bagTag);
    }
    String loadedLegId = bag.loadedLegId();
    LegRow loadedLeg = null;
    if (loadedLegId != null) {
        // 与封舱/排舱串行：先持航段行锁再持行李行锁，与装载链路锁序一致
        loadedLeg = lockLeg(loadedLegId);
    }
    bag = lockBag(bagTag);
    WeightRow profile = findWeight(bagTag);
    if (profile == null) 404;
    version check 409;
    if (bag.loadedLegId() != null) {
        // 以持锁后的最新状态判定
        if (loadedLeg == null || !loadedLeg.legId().equals(bag.loadedLegId())) {
            loadedLeg = lockLeg(bag.loadedLegId());  // hmm, leg→bag order violated again
        }
        ...
    }
}
```

This gets messy. Pragmatic approach: after locking leg (if loadedLegId from initial read) and then bag, use the bag's current loadedLegId:
- if null now → bag was unloaded; no checks needed.
- if equals locked leg → do checks.
- if different → extremely rare race; we could throw 409 conflict asking retry. That's safe and simple: "行李装载状态变化，请重试" 409. Acceptable.

